SESSION RECORD 2026-07-29 (office bootstrap + dexter->nomac). Filed by FRONT DOOR because check-project-busy realisateur reported BUSY (foreign interactive claude pid 3219736) for the entire close, so .scheduler/FOCUS.md could not be written directly -- closeout-lint FLAG [no-record] is therefore UNRESOLVED BY DESIGN, and the fix when the lock clears is: focus-commit realisateur <msgfile> .scheduler/FOCUS.md with this payload. WHAT HAPPENED: (1) dexter cleared to bare (scheduler clone removed; realisateur fd451a4, 0db3830, 2940b37 hold the notes). (2) New repo media-arts-collective/office built and pushed -- handbook, work-order/commissio/mail/wages protocols, hash-chained ledger, isometric floor, plus a WORKING loopback SMTP transport with a 17-assertion acceptance contract (office f63ce49, f9198dc, d79e166). (3) Office moved off dexter onto nomac, a new Ubuntu 24.04.4 VirtualBox guest (hostfwd 2224), landed by script, contract 17/17 there; dexter footprint fully retired and verified; senechal 719dd0f, 0bf6ad7, 350a311 carry the machine-config declarations. FINDINGS worth keeping: a deploy script's value is not saving keystrokes, it is that the SECOND host disagrees with the first -- moving hosts found three defects one host had hidden (systemd --user cannot use ProtectKernelTunables/Modules/ControlGroups -> 218/CAPABILITIES; a version check comparing strings as floats so 3.12 read older than 3.9; node/claude miscategorised as fatal when they are the employees' runtime, not the office's). One config source is not enough if the READER drops the assignment: office.conf declared GROUPS=, a bash special readonly array, so the assignment vanished with no error and bootstrap created a mailbox named 1000 while reporting success -- bootstrap now probes every key for that collision class. "The port is open" was never the check: the first VM waiter fired 20s into a 5min install because subiquity's own installer sshd answers on the forwarded port. And the environment that refuses you the convenient dependency is testing your bootstrap, not obstructing you -- no sudo/pip/MTA on dexter is exactly why the transport is stdlib-only and can be stood up unattended. DECISIONS filed to scheduler BLOCKERS.md d60c928 (two personnel documents; claude auth on nomac). NOT MINE, left untouched: bibliothecaire dirty tree (BUSY, pid 3216059) including an 18KB office personnel-manual draft from that live session.
